{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"9b77fca3437450ae","type":"text","text":"## **Original novel | Chapter V: Advice from a Caterpillar**\n*Lewis Carroll, Alice’s Adventures in Wonderland (1865)*\n\n> The Caterpillar and Alice looked at each other for some time in silence: at last the Caterpillar took the hookah out of its mouth, and addressed her in a languid, sleepy voice.\n\n> ‘Who are you?’ said the Caterpillar.\n\n> This was not an encouraging opening for a conversation. Alice replied, rather shyly, ‘I--I hardly know, sir, just at present-- at least I know who I was when I got up this morning, but I think I must have been changed several times since then.’\n\n> ‘What do you mean by that?’ said the Caterpillar sternly. ‘Explain yourself!’\n\n> ‘I can't explain myself, I'm afraid, sir’ said Alice, ‘because I'm not myself, you see.’\n\n> ‘I don't see,’ said the Caterpillar.\n\n> ‘I'm afraid I can't put it more clearly,’ Alice replied very politely, ‘for I can't understand it myself to begin with; and being so many different sizes in a day is very confusing.’","x":1140,"y":-335,"width":830,"height":705},
		{"id":"402bcb23fd2a4e4e","type":"text","text":"## **Context and vocabulary support**\nAlice has changed size several times and meets a Caterpillar who asks a difficult question.\n\n**Mini-glossary outside the original:**\n*Caterpillar* = rups\n*languid* = loom\n*sternly* = streng\n\n","x":1140,"y":400,"width":830,"height":235,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"0e33ba0e43cf7d50","type":"text","text":"# **Todays Class**\n### Alice in Wonderland | Lesson 2 of 3","x":-812,"y":-558,"width":650,"height":110,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"138f1cb64f85567b","type":"text","text":" \n### **08:15** - Introduction: The Caterpillar\n\n### **08:20**  Read and skim \n\n### **08:30**  Word meaning + false friends \n### **08:35 min**  Grammar + advice \n### **08:45 min**  Exit ticket ","x":-812,"y":-418,"width":650,"height":278,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"f3fa5a630ebd8478","type":"text","text":"# **Homework** for the 27th of November\nWrite a **8-line dialogue** between Alice and a friend.\n\nUse **one present perfect form** and **two modals**.\n\nUpload at least **2 unfamiliar words** in google classroom from the passage we discussed.","x":-812,"y":-126,"width":650,"height":200,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"c561b76ddf92a784","type":"text","text":"**Read the original conversation**\nListen to the voices: who sounds **shy**? Who sounds **stern**?\n\n**Q2:** skim the passage. Choose **A, B or C** and write only the letter.","x":2293,"y":-319,"width":630,"height":200,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"f76f50a883a72729","type":"text","text":"**TASK + evidence in pairs**\n**Q3:** copy **ONE short phrase** showing that Alice feels unsure.\n**Q4:** explain whether *copy* allows a Dutch translation. **Yes/no + 5–10 English words.**\n**Q5:** match *sternly*, *confusing*, *at present* with their meanings.","x":2293,"y":-91,"width":630,"height":230,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"574ad03e2c5f638c","type":"text","text":"**False-friend detective**\n**Q6:** choose what **eventually** and **actual** mean in the *new* examples.\n\n","x":2293,"y":167,"width":630,"height":174,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"09bfc34f7f5de3c1","type":"text","text":"**Individual language lab**\n**Q7:** complete TWO sentences with **has + past participle** (*change*, *ask*).\n**Q8:** write one kind sentence with **should / could**, plus one with **doesn’t have to**.\n\n","x":2293,"y":370,"width":630,"height":218,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"0bdc494487051592","type":"text","text":"**Exit ticket: Q9**\nName Alice’s feeling in **ONE word** and give **ONE exact clue** from the text.","x":2293,"y":617,"width":630,"height":164,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"44a5f97dd3995de7","type":"text","text":"## **Big question**\nWho are you? Why does Alice struggle to answer?","x":158,"y":-360,"width":600,"height":112,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"a5436460730e2406","type":"text","text":"## **Learning goals**\n**I can:** \n- explain Alice’s problem; \n- copy **one** clue; \n- infer tone from words; \n- recognise false friends; \n- Have practiced the present perfect and supportive modals.","x":158,"y":-219,"width":600,"height":193,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"41c61f19364c69e2","type":"text","text":"**Retrieval**\nWhat happened to Alice in Lesson 1? \n\n**| Prediction**\nDo **Q1**: write **one possible reason** someone might feel confused about who they are.","x":158,"y":-2,"width":600,"height":186,"color":"3"}
	],
